	(text "output Capacitor seletion:\n1.filters inductor current at output\n2.supports load support before regulator can react\n	"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240.538 56.642 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "fa5c8c71-5768-42fc-b255-daac50496f5c")
	)
	(text "Note: for CCM\nA synchronous half-bridge with a gate driver, not a diode. This is what makes forced CCM possible at all. With a Schottky, the board goes DCM below about 0.3-0.36 A and you can't fix it in firmware.\nBipolar current sensing. The sense amp needs a mid-supply bias (about 1.65 V on a 3.3 V ADC) so it can read negative inductor current at light load.\nInductor footprint with some flexibility. Choose a footprint that fits both 100 µH and 120 µH parts, or a bit larger, in case you want to swap values later."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.486 151.384 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ffbf774f-baa4-427a-9178-625ab6eb8696")
	)
